# armour/man/plate: steel plate on the man (P2c, SLICE-ARMOUR; re-shaded by LADDER-ARMOUR for the ladder, STYLE_P2 25.2,
# 27.5): a gorget, a breastplate in broad planes with a DEEP shadow side (the owner: "pale and flat"): the lit plane (step 3)
# is a narrow band at the top-left, the turn (step 2) one column, and the shadow side (step 1) half the plate; ONE lit
# ridge (a step-4 run on the keel facing down, on the lit edge facing right and left); a fauld lame under the belt.
# Finish regions (contracts 3b): R the gorget's rim and the fauld's hem, P the breastplate's centre, G the chest socket
# (3x2 facing down, 2x2 facing left / right), N the breastplate's lower edge, W one 2x2 spot on the shadow side.
# Keys: rest idle run runl drawn swing lie in D U R L (side runl: the run's lean rows); the L lie is the lying chest.
# Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h. Source: LADDER-ARMOUR's expand.py (one rest view per facing).
# (LADDER-ARMOUR i3) N (T6 runes) only on the breastplate's lower edge: one designed rune band, not specks over the gorget,
# the chest and the tassets (the blind panel: "scattered 1px specks that look like noise").
# (LADDER-ARMOUR polish i3) T5 wears its people's colour: the surcoat in the accent slot (tabardColor), the skirt's
# cross gilt, so T5 reads red-and-gold, the Mythic white-black-and-fire, T6 blue-and-silver (the panel: "T5 and Mythic
# both red and gold, one outline").
# (LADDER-ARMOUR alloys i1) the T4 plate in broad lit planes for ANY metal (the owner: "T3->T4 the weakest step"):
# a lit pec plane with a 2-px step-4 specular, one keel ridge, the shadow half, a dark underside row and a lit fauld lame.
# (LADDER-ARMOUR alloys i1) the Mythic body in its own BLACKENED steel (metal slot, kind 11), not linen: the
# owner saw a white slab with no dark values; dark plate, white-hot edges, gold trim and fire carry it.
# (LADDER-ARMOUR alloys i2) T5's breast is its METAL again: a cuirass (lit left plane, a step-4 glint, the shadow side)
# under a gilt neckline and chevron, the people's colour kept below the belt, on the cloak and the plume (the panels:
# "the red tabard covers ~60% of the sprite, only helm, pauldrons and legs show the alloy").
# (LADDER-ARMOUR alloys i3) the Mythic blackened plate's lit plane a step brighter (the left two fifths, the light side):
# polished black steel with a dark core on the shadow side, not a flat mid grey (the panels: "Mythic reads darker
# and muddier than T6 at game scale").
use person
body man
role armour plate
layer torso
anchor neck
keys torso
z 2
legend Q linen 0
legend R linen 1
legend S linen 2
legend T linen 3
legend U linen 4
legend J cloak 0
legend D cloak 1
legend H cloak 2
legend I cloak 3
legend X cloak 4
legend k device 1
legend l device 2
legend F device 3

